# Foreign Entity Registration — Upon Award Only (TPA)

**Dee Davis Inc. does NOT foreign-qualify in a state because an opportunity exists there. That is not how a contract management TPA operates.**

## The Rule

**Default: NO foreign entity filing until a contract is awarded AND qualification is required to perform, invoice, or enroll.**

Foreign qualification is **post-award compliance overhead** — not bid prep, not pipeline hygiene, not "get ready just in case."

```
Bid / pursue opportunity → NO SOS foreign filing
Award + performance requires in-state qual → MI good standing → ONE state filing → operate
```

## Why (TPA Model)

- DDI is **Michigan domestic** — SAM-registered, nationwide TPA. Bidding does not require 50-state SOS registrations.
- Fulfillment is dispatched under DDI contract management — **not** "we must exist as a foreign corp everywhere we might bid."
- SOS fees ($30–$750+; NV ~$725+ stack) are **recovered from contract revenue**, not speculative spend before award.

## When Filing IS Allowed

| Trigger | Action |
|---|---|
| **Contract awarded** and performance/invoicing/enrollment requires foreign qual | File in **that state only** — see `NEXUS_LEARNING/FOREIGN_ENTITY_REGISTRATION_FEES_50_STATES.md` |
| **Solicitation pass/fail** requires foreign qualification **with the proposal** | File before submit — **only** if the RFP explicitly requires it |
| **Award letter / kickoff** requires qual before start date | File in award week, before first invoice/trip/enrollment step |

## When Filing Is FORBIDDEN (NEXUS Must Not Suggest)

- ❌ "Register in [State] so you can bid this RFP"
- ❌ "Cheap fee — file now while you're pursuing"
- ❌ "Pre-qualify in FL/TX/LA for HAVEN pipeline" before any award
- ❌ Adding foreign qual as a **pre-bid workflow step** in `WORKFLOW_CHECKLIST.md` unless solicitation requires it at proposal
- ❌ Treating `FOREIGN_ENTITY_REGISTRATION_FEES_50_STATES.md` as a to-do list

## Bid / Proposal Language (Default)

When a state may eventually require qualification but **not at proposal**:

> Dee Davis Inc. will complete foreign qualification in [State] upon contract award, prior to performance start, in compliance with [State] requirements.

Do **not** imply DDI is already foreign-qualified in that state unless it is.

## Revenue Analysis

- May note **estimated post-award SOS fee** as a one-time performance cost after win — **not** as a bid-stage action item.
- Do **not** block GO/NO-GO on "haven't filed foreign entity yet" unless the solicitation requires qual at submission.

## Known Post-Award Gates (Not Pre-Bid)

| Lane | Note |
|---|---|
| NY (e.g. SUNY / county invoice address) | File **after** award path confirms NY invoicing requirement — not because RFP is open |
| MD Medicaid | Foreign qual is enrollment gate — **after** MD contract/Medicaid path is real |
| Any state | File **before first invoice or regulated activity** in that state — not before bid |

## Source of Truth for Fees (After Award Only)

`NEXUS_LEARNING/FOREIGN_ENTITY_REGISTRATION_FEES_50_STATES.md` — lookup when a **win** triggers filing. Re-check SOS link the week you file.

